We need to output a full HTML file implementing the game. Must be self-contained, inline CSS and JS, canvas 2D, requestAnimationFrame with delta time, keyboard + on-screen buttons, localStorage best score with try/catch.

Implement game logic:

- Game area 16:9 letterboxed. We'll set canvas width/height based on window size, maintain aspect ratio 16:9. Use devicePixelRatio for crispness.

- Objects: types: red cube, blue cylinder, yellow egg. Each has x position (start at left), y on belt. Belt moves right at speed based on level.

- Bins: three bins at bottom right side, each colored and labelled.

- Gripper: hangs from gantry at top, can move left/right. Has open/closed state. When lowered, if not holding and collides with object, it grabs (holds). If holding and space pressed again, opens and drops object at current x (vertical drop). If not holding and space pressed, lower; if reaches object (i.e., y reaches object top), close and lift.

- Fast drop: pressing space twice quickly (within e.g., 0.3 sec) while lowering onto an egg triggers break. Implementation: track lastSpacePressTime; if second press within threshold while gripper is moving down and not holding, set fastDrop flag for that lowering. If fastDrop and object is egg, break.

Simplify: When space pressed and gripper is up (not lowered), start lowering. If space pressed again while lowering (i.e., before reaching object), treat as fast drop: set fastDrop = true. If fastDrop and object is egg, break.

- Lives: 3 icons.

- Score: +10 per correct sort, +5 combo bonus each after three consecutive correct sorts without losing a life. So track comboCount; when comboCount reaches 3, add +5 and reset? Actually "three correct sorts in a row without losing a life gives +5 bonus each." Means each correct sort after reaching 3 in a row gives +5? Could interpret: after each correct sort, if you have at least 3 consecutive correct sorts, you get +5 bonus. We'll implement: comboStreak increments on correct sort, resets on mistake. If comboStreak >=3, add +5 bonus each correct sort.

- Belt speed: base speed, increase after every 5 sorted objects (sortedCount). Level = floor(sortedCount/5)+1. Speed = base * (1 + 0.1*(level-1)).

- Objects spawn at left at intervals, maybe every 1.5 seconds, random type.

- When object reaches right end (x > beltEnd), it's a miss: lose life, remove object.

- When dropping object: if x within bin's x range, check color match. If correct: score +10, sortedCount++, particle burst, comboStreak++. If wrong: lose life, comboStreak=0, maybe particle.

- If dropping onto floor (outside bins) also lose life.

- When gripper holds object and space pressed: open jaws and drop object at current x (vertical). The object will fall down; we can just evaluate drop instantly (no physics) for simplicity.

- Gripper movement: left/right arrows or A/D, also on-screen buttons.

- On-screen buttons: three buttons: left, right, down (space). Also restart button.

- Start screen: title, goal, controls. Any key or click starts.

- Win screen: when sortedCount >=20: show "Line cleared!", final score, best score, "Press R to play again". Also restart button.

- Lose screen: lives <=0: "Line stopped", final score, best score, "Press R to retry". Also restart button.

- Best score stored in localStorage under key "gripperRushBest". Use try/catch.

- No console errors.

Implementation details:

Canvas scaling: function resizeCanvas() sets canvas.width = window.innerWidth * dpr, canvas.height = window.innerHeight * dpr, then set style width/height to window.innerWidth/Height. Compute scale = Math.min(width/16, height/9) to maintain 16:9 letterbox. We'll draw with a transform: ctx.translate(marginX, marginY); ctx.scale(scale, scale); then draw in virtual coordinates of 16x9.

Game loop: requestAnimationFrame with deltaTime.

Objects: array of {type, x, y, width, height}. Belt y constant.

Gripper: x position (center), y (top). When lowered, y increases until reaches object top (object.y - object.height). We'll have state: gripperState = 'up' | 'down' | 'holding'. When space pressed and state up: start lowering (targetY = object under gripper? Actually we need to detect if there is an object directly below gripper. We'll check for any object whose x range includes gripper x and whose y is below gripper. If found, set targetY = object.y - object.height - small offset. If not, lower to belt level (just above belt). When reaches targetY, if object present, close jaws and hold object (set holding = object). If fastDrop and object.type == 'egg', break egg: remove object, lose life, particle crack.

If gripper is holding and space pressed: open jaws, drop object at current x: evaluate bin. Then set holding = null, gripperState = 'up'.

Simplify: We'll not animate vertical drop of object; just evaluate instantly.

Fast drop detection: When space pressed while gripper is moving down (state 'down'), set fastDrop = true. If fastDrop and object is egg, break.

But we need to know which object is being targeted. We'll store currentTargetObject when lowering starts.

Implementation steps:

- Variables: score, sortedCount, lives, comboStreak, beltLevel, beltSpeed, objects array, gripperX, gripperY, gripperState, holdingObject, fastDrop, lastSpaceTime.

- Spawn timer.

- Update: move objects by beltSpeed * dt. Remove off-screen.

- Gripper movement: left/right with speed.

- Input handling: keydown events.

- Buttons: click/touch.

- Drawing: background dark, conveyor belt rectangle, bins, objects, gripper (two jaws), HUD, particles.

- Particles: array of {x,y,vx,vy,lifetime,color}. On correct sort, burst. On egg break, crack effect: maybe draw crack lines.

- Crack effect: simple: draw a few lines on egg before removal.

Simplify: When egg breaks, create particles with yellow color and draw a crack (two lines) at egg position for a short time.

We'll implement particles with update and draw.

Edge Cases: Ensure no errors when localStorage unavailable.

Now produce final HTML. Ensure no external resources.

